From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenATV <openatv@openatv.org>
Date: Fri, 14 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system/linux/openat2.h: fix conflict with glibc 2.43

glibc 2.43 now declares openat2() in <bits/fcntl-linux.h> as an
extern function. MPD's own static inline openat2() wrapper conflicts
with this declaration, causing a compile error:

  error: 'int openat2(...)' was declared 'extern' and later 'static'

Guard the local definition so it is only used when glibc does not
provide openat2() (i.e. __GLIBC_PREREQ < 2.43).

---
 src/system/linux/openat2.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/system/linux/openat2.h b/src/system/linux/openat2.h
--- a/src/system/linux/openat2.h
+++ b/src/system/linux/openat2.h
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
 #include <unistd.h>

+#if !defined(__GLIBC_PREREQ) || !__GLIBC_PREREQ(2, 43)
+
 static inline int
 openat2(int dirfd, const char *pathname,
 	const struct open_how *how, size_t size)
@@ -17,3 +19,5 @@ openat2(int dirfd, const char *pathname,
 {
 	return syscall(__NR_openat2, dirfd, pathname, how, size);
 }
+
+#endif
